  "title": "Venezuela Lake Maracaibo 504 oil slick detections (Jan 2025–Mar 2026)",
  "url": "https://globalwitness.org/en/campaigns/fossil-fuels/ecocide-in-venezuela-oil-mining-and-the-risks-of-foreign-investment/",
  "snippet": "Global Witness report documents 504 oil slick detections in Lake Maracaibo, Venezuela between January 2025 and March 2026, using SkyTruth Cerulean data derived from Sentinel-1A C-band SAR imagery. The report labels the situation an 'ecocide' driven by aging PDVSA infrastructure, chronic pipeline leaks, and lack of maintenance. Lake Maracaibo, one of the world's oldest and largest lakes, faces severe ecological damage. The report also highlights risks to foreign investors considering partnerships with Venezuela's oil sector.",
